From 39c79c3c528ec149b091caeb063d3b6a53f3c8a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: permissionBRICK <40219477+permissionBRICK@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:25:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 30/31] ASoC: codecs: lpass-wsa-macro: register the mclk output
 with devm

The WSA macro registered its mclk output with clk_hw_register() and never unregistered it. A second probe, after an
unbind, failed with -EEXIST ("failed to register clk 'mclk'"). On the ASUS Vivobook S 15 (X1E80100) the WSA macros
are unbound and probed again whenever the ADSP restarts (hibernation), so the speakers stayed silent afterwards. The
RX, TX and VA macros already use devm_clk_hw_register().

Not upstream.
---
 sound/soc/codecs/lpass-wsa-macro.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-wsa-macro.c b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-wsa-macro.c
index fecc4a425..9d5ac0319 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-wsa-macro.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-wsa-macro.c
@@ -2659,7 +2659,7 @@ static int wsa_macro_register_mclk_output(struct wsa_macro *wsa)
 	init.num_parents = 1;
 	wsa->hw.init = &init;
 	hw = &wsa->hw;
-	ret = clk_hw_register(wsa->dev, hw);
+	ret = devm_clk_hw_register(wsa->dev, hw);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
